# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# URL canonicalization: extension-less page requests → their .html
# file, via a real 301 redirect.
#
# These are explicit, literal "from" paths (no :placeholders / *splats).
# That is deliberate: the previous rules used
#   /:page              /:page.html              200
#   /:folder/:page      /:folder/:page.html      200
#   /:folder/:sub/:page /:folder/:sub/:page.html 200
# which silently rewrote (status 200) ANY unmatched path to "<path>.html",
# creating a second live, indexable URL for every page with no canonical
# HTTP signal. Simply flipping those same placeholder rules to 301 is
# NOT safe: a placeholder like :page matches a full path segment
# including dots, so a mistyped/nonexistent URL that already ends in
# ".html" (e.g. /foo.html) would ALSO match, get redirected to
# "/foo.html.html", which again matches the same rule, and so on —
# an infinite redirect loop. Existing real .html files never hit these
# rules (Netlify serves an existing static file before evaluating
# _redirects), so this file only needs to list the extension-less
# alias for each real public page. Anything not listed here simply
# falls through to the site's normal 404 handling (see netlify.toml),
# exactly as it would for any other nonexistent path.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

